WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
The Earth's surface gives
off infrared radiation.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.650
Nitrogen molecules let
it pass straight through.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.430
Carbon dioxide molecules
hold some of it back,

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.410
then send it out again in all directions.

5
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:18.230
So why does carbon dioxide trap heat,
while nitrogen, most of the air, does not?

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.290
In this mission, you'll read
the mass spectrum of a molecule,

7
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.050
and use the masses lost to work
out the pieces it breaks into.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:30.890
You'll read infrared spectra, and use
their bands to identify functional groups.

9
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.830
Your mission: explain why carbon dioxide
is a greenhouse gas, but nitrogen is not.
